#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348618 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given an Arbitrary Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbb9e2ef-e6f4-5842-a54f-22a5a581cf07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}(4^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbb9e2ef-e6f4-5842-a54f-22a5a581cf07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}(4^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348620} :answer-field/id #uuid "6171aebd-b144-5756-9dde-eb8785171ba3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5731125-307e-51c6-9f9a-f16cf62d6761" :question/math-academy-id "q-276486" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $320$ and the common ratio is $4?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 320 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 320 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(1-{4}^{N})}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}({4}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Few Terms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f21bd8b-579f-572e-827a-1f5096bffa1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348623} {:answer/id #uuid "a669d986-b3bd-5d5d-abae-1611c020cf6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}(1-{5}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348624} {:answer/id #uuid "4073891e-8a98-5727-9414-3b1801fbe3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}({3}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348625} {:answer/id #uuid "e81f080b-0b8c-5f3f-88dd-050066b91727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}(1-{3}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348626} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1a2642-e2b7-5b7d-abbe-5ebb9e7f8598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({5}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f21bd8b-579f-572e-827a-1f5096bffa1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348623} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd5b44dc-ca0f-5f74-81cc-6b5116cc8922" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "968d763f-7575-5b03-8e25-e8e3c2bafb23" :question/math-academy-id "q-39996" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $3+15+75+⋯\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=5.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{5}^{N})}{1-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{5}^{N})}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(1-{5}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given an Arbitrary Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c856e8d0-7aa7-5451-8e1d-432d7978f28a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{N}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348630} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee4b3bb-2e41-5c34-8d7a-5d57d77bf837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{N}-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348631} {:answer/id #uuid "3955e9ec-c0be-5304-aa2f-c1504cba7382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({3}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348632} {:answer/id #uuid "a87447b3-4978-57b6-88e3-a3b4fc692a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3({4}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348633} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9fe08c-7ac4-5c96-8a4a-2c0643379b7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{N}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c856e8d0-7aa7-5451-8e1d-432d7978f28a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{N}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348630} :answer-field/id #uuid "9124a7fe-87cf-5f88-be2b-e8c915c23b03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "595b4600-8002-5fc9-aae5-7663d61dcae3" :question/math-academy-id "q-67104" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $192$ and the common ratio is $4?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 192 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 192 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{3(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & ={4}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given an Arbitrary Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2389d4a2-b843-5528-9175-9f2fd09ff939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({4}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348637} {:answer/id #uuid "ea7adb18-dbfe-5840-975c-125e7a68beeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{N}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348638} {:answer/id #uuid "25f2836d-01f8-5701-bb63-b68b0ebfdda2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{N}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348639} {:answer/id #uuid "2c5301bb-0b79-5e78-8fd1-fddf6a2df8db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3({4}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348640} {:answer/id #uuid "b999a01c-f4e0-5c76-83d4-2036f54dc55b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{N}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2389d4a2-b843-5528-9175-9f2fd09ff939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({4}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348637} :answer-field/id #uuid "92b18c56-2e57-5839-acc8-ce5670f616a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9360a987-6868-5ee3-a005-1b57385aa970" :question/math-academy-id "q-73425" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $384$ and the common ratio is $4?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{3} \\\\ 384 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-2(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =2({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348642 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Few Terms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7de65e78-fe90-5a32-9cb1-0301bdc86afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\frac{4}{6})}^{N}+\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348644} {:answer/id #uuid "8581926b-a68e-50bd-bb10-4e76f852d381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\frac{4}{6})}^{N}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348645} {:answer/id #uuid "e1338150-8dee-5635-b2b7-90b6e36e1bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}(1-{4}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348646} {:answer/id #uuid "d88b3f06-dc91-56da-972c-ee6f11e78f2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348647} {:answer/id #uuid "4d59f86f-91a9-5d13-9756-4acbc5a06541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d88b3f06-dc91-56da-972c-ee6f11e78f2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348647} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bd95049-5642-5a48-968c-70603aa94243" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "78fba3be-7310-5e50-9e3c-f6710527699a" :question/math-academy-id "q-9749" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a series $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+⋯?$" :question/worked-solution "Note that $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+⋯$ is the sum of a geometric series since the ratio of any two consecutive terms is constant.\n\nFirst, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $r=4.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{3}\\cdot ({4}^{N}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
